  {
   "id": "w03saCpoBAAJ",
   "from": "Mike Collyer",
   "author": "aab55242ff4da6c6",
   "date": "2018-01-24T23:58:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] 2-block PLS with single variable",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Chris,<div><br></div><div>It does not matter interns of the math and it should not matter in terms of the function but if it works one way you can be sure it’s the same result as switching the order, if the function worked. The error is because the function is trying to multiply matrices and in this case, y is a vector. This means we fail to coerce a vector into a matrix on either the left side or the ride side, but do so the other way around. </div><div><br></div><div>We will have to check for that error but you can feel confident that it does not make a difference. </div><div><br></div><div>Mike<br><br><div>Sent from my iPhone</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div><div><br>On Jan 24, 2018, at 6:47 PM, Chris Law &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cj...@ucsc.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Hi all,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">I have a somewhat silly question. When running a 2-block PLS between a landmark dataset (shape3D) and a single variable (BF), does the order of the blocks matter? </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">I ask because the function runs smoothly with <i>phylo.integration(<b>BF, shape3D</b>, tree_prune, iter=999)</i></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div><font face=\"georgia, serif\">but running<i> phylo.integration(</i></font><i style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><b>shape3D</b></i><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><i><b>, BF</b> , tree_prune, iter=999) </i>leds to this error: Error in y %*% V : non-conformable arguments</font></div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">I am trying to examine how cranial shape is associated with bite force (BF), essentially hoping to find a linear combination of shape variables that predicts BF. So I&#39;m hoping to run a model that resembles BF ~ shape3D.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">I greatly appreciate your help.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Best,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\">Chris</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div><b><br></b></div><div><b>Chris Law<div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\">​ </div></b><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\">|</span><b><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\"> ​</div></b><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\">Graduate Student</span><b><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\"> </div></b><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\">|</span><b><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\"> ​</div></b><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\">University of California, Santa Cruz</span><div style=\"font-size:12.6667px;font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\">​ </div></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Coastal Biology Building<div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;display:inline\">​</div></span></div></div><div style=\"font-size:small\">130 McAllister Way </div><div style=\"font-size:small\">Santa Cruz, CA 95060</div><a href style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-size:small\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cj...@ucsc.edu</a><span style=\"font-size:small\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\">|</span><span style=\"font-size:12.6667px\"> </span><a href=\"http://research.pbsci.ucsc.edu/eeb/cjlaw/\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-size:12.8px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://research.pbsci.ucsc.edu/eeb/cjlaw/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485866426000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12loHu6I7MWNzS4-1Dl5Mb\">http://research.pbsci.ucsc.edu/eeb/cjlaw/</a><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"> <br></span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
